{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Evidence: the crash is intermittent, not a deterministic regression\n\n`build-and-test / pytest (ubuntu-latest, py3.11)` **passed** on `main` at the same\ncommit the crash was observed against.\n\n- Crashing run: 35510440501 (change 3008 patch set 1, rev `f2200580a17e`), py3.11 leg\n  crashed `gw3` on `test_worker_cancellation_survives_job_completion_race`.\n- Passing run: 35511654149 `Test Suite (mirror)`, head `e84e4c5e943`, job\n  106080485643 `build-and-test / pytest (ubuntu-latest, py3.11)` -> **success**.\n\n`f2200580a17e` is change 3008 applied on top of `e84e4c5e943`, and change 3008 touches\nonly `.github/workflows/external-integration.yml`. So the two runs exercise effectively\nidentical Python code on the same interpreter leg, and one crashed while the other did\nnot.\n\nThis rules out a deterministic regression of `8c9bf5d78d` and confirms the failure is a\nlow-rate race. It also means a reproduction attempt must be a LOOP, not a single run --\none green run is not evidence of absence. The prior RCA's own oracle needed 3 runs to\nshow 2 hangs, so the historical rate is high enough to catch in tens of runs but not in\none.\n\n## Sweep context\n\n`main` currently carries no other unexplained CI failure. Non-green runs as of\n2026-09-20T13:15Z:\n\n| Run | Workflow | State | Attribution |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 35510440501 | change 3008 Verified gate | failure | THIS ticket |\n| 35507409132 | Terraform Drift | failure | known, awaiting user decision (`[rebar:3d85-eaad-b5e0-4f84]`) |\n| 35508005436 | Live External Integration | in progress | healthy; DC harness at 1h43m vs a 6252s green baseline |\n| 35511654149 | Test Suite (mirror) | in progress | py3.11 leg already green |\n| 35512947017 | Mirror Guard | in progress | - |\n\nA differential reproduction on a dedicated Python 3.11.16 environment is now running\n(the repo `.venv` is 3.12.14 and cannot discriminate a 3.11-only defect).\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789910187800549852,"uuid":"4013154a-65aa-4b2d-bbc7-8ae1ba832d7f"}